WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.960
A superhero mockumentary, a missing god, and MCU&nbsp;
storylines fans thought had been forgotten — all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.896
told in 15 minutes or less! These are the&nbsp;
Marvel One-shot films, ranked worst to best.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.160
The Consultant, coming out with&nbsp;
the home video release of Thor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.160
is basically just Agent Coulson and Agent Sitwell&nbsp;
talking in a restaurant booth for three minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.400
Plus, there's the mid-credits scene from The&nbsp;
Incredible Hulk sandwiched in for context.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.120
That scene, featuring Tony Stark approaching&nbsp;
General Thunderbolt Ross about a new hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.240
joining the Avenger Initiative, is the basis of&nbsp;
the entire short film. It seems that the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.760
Security Council thinks Emil Blonsky, a.k.a. the&nbsp;
Abomination, would be a worthy addition to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.880
team of heroes they're assembling. But, Coulson&nbsp;
and Sitwell disagree. They need someone to pitch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:52.560
Blonsky's recruitment who Ross will probably&nbsp;
refuse. Enter Stark, a.k.a. "The Consultant."

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:58.480
This One-Shot barely justifies its existence and&nbsp;
finds itself at a point in the MCU timeline where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.280
anyone unfamiliar with the franchise likely&nbsp;
won't get it. One could argue that this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.560
the very purpose of the One-Shot program; to&nbsp;
expand the MCU by filling in gaps with smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.760
stories that don't have to appeal to the masses.&nbsp;
Still, the script of The Consultant is bogged down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.880
with fast dialogue and name-drops that only&nbsp;
hardcore fans will be able to follow. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.440
at barely three minutes, it hardly has time to&nbsp;
make that much of an impression. Regardless, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.727
the first time up to bat for the One-Shot program,&nbsp;
it's a perfectly acceptable proof of concept.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.840
Item 47 was revealed on the Blu-ray and&nbsp;
digital release of The Avengers. Taking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.640
place immediately after the events of the film,&nbsp;
this Marvel One-Shot is the tale of a couple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.840
Bennie and Claire, who steal a Chitauri weapon&nbsp;
in the aftermath of the big Battle of New York.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.120
Using the weapon as leverage, they scour the East&nbsp;
Coast and rob bank after bank to rack up cash.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.840
Agent Sitwell makes it his&nbsp;
mission to track them down;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.760
but rather than punishing them, he&nbsp;
gives them jobs at SHIELD instead.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.800
At 11 minutes, Item 47 has time to flesh&nbsp;
out its story and two main characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.720
They both make their Marvel debut here,&nbsp;
but are subsequently never seen again in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:10.000
any further MCU production. Director Louis&nbsp;
D'Esposito shares in the book The Story of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.960
Marvel Studios that the Disney CEO Bob Iger liked&nbsp;
the pitch for Item 47 so much that he suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:22.720
it be expanded into a television series. This&nbsp;
led to Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. on ABC. Oddly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.760
though, Bennie and Claire never appeared on that&nbsp;
show. Item 47 constantly feels like it's building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.320
toward something, but never really arrives&nbsp;
anywhere. However, that feeling might only be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:37.334
because most Marvel projects have trained viewers&nbsp;
to expect everything to lead into the next film.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.560
This mockumentary is a fun twist on the typical&nbsp;
tone of the MCU and feels more like an episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.920
of The Office. Team Thor: Part One was released&nbsp;
alongside the home video debut of Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.840
Civil War, but was also widely circulated on an&nbsp;
official Marvel YouTube channel. The majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.200
MCU superheroes at the time were divided into&nbsp;
either Team Iron Man or Team Captain America.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.440
Because, if you remember, the two Avengers&nbsp;
faced off against each other in Captain America:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.640
Civil War. This One-Shot attempts to explain&nbsp;
the absence of Thor, and subsequently Hulk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.760
from the Civil War action. It turns out Thor&nbsp;
has settled down in an apartment in Australia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.000
living a relatively subdued life in&nbsp;
comparison to his heroic feats of yore.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.480
"I’ll just start my own team. Team Thor,&nbsp;
of course. It would be me… and Darryl."

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.560
Directed by Taika Waititi, who would later take&nbsp;
on Thor: Ragnarok and Thor: Love and Thunder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.200
this One-Shot is an irreverent deviation&nbsp;
from the norm of a Marvel story in style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.640
technique, and narrative.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.280
With an appearance by Mark Ruffalo, the story&nbsp;
of Team Thor might break the continuity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.240
Hulk's arc, depending on if Marvel considers&nbsp;
this One-Shot canon. At the end of Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.960
Age of Ultron, Hulk blasts into space and&nbsp;
seems to stay there until the events of Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.240
Ragnarok. This One-Shot takes place between&nbsp;
those films, but features Hulk on Earth.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:04:00.320
The second One-Shot ever made, A Funny&nbsp;
Thing Happened On The Way To Thor's Hammer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.160
came out with the home video release&nbsp;
of Captain America: The First Avenger.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.040
It takes place just prior to the events of Thor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.520
Agent Coulson travels to the middle of the&nbsp;
American desert to examine Thor's hammer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.960
which at this point in the story had just dropped&nbsp;
from the sky with unexplained mystical properties.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:21.840
Mjolnir's owner had not yet arrived on Earth,&nbsp;
and Agent Coulson's team was managing its care.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.320
On the way to the hammer, Coulson stops at&nbsp;
a gas station, where he inadvertently breaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.960
up a robbery in true SHIELD fashion. While&nbsp;
brief, this One-Shot features a fun action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.120
scene for Agent Coulson. It's an example of&nbsp;
something that works within the context of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:41.040
the MCU timeline while simultaneously making for&nbsp;
an enjoyable, low-stakes short film. It's even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.323
fun if it's viewed by someone detached from any&nbsp;
familiarity with Coulson or even Marvel itself.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:51.680
A similarly styled follow-up to the original,&nbsp;
Team Thor: Part Two is a mockumentary showing Thor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.800
biding out his time on Earth during the events of&nbsp;
Captain America: Civil War. In a way, this proves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.720
that Thor could have thrived in the laid-back&nbsp;
atmosphere of New Asgard we see him in during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:05.280
the middle of Avengers: Endgame. The scenarios&nbsp;
in that film and this One-Shot are the same:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.000
Thor grounding himself in non-hero living. The&nbsp;
difference is whether he chooses to put mind over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.440
matter. In Team Thor, he seems to thrive. In&nbsp;
Avengers: Endgame, he wallows in self-pity.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:19.360
Given the straight-laced mockumentary&nbsp;
format of Team Thor, it's fascinating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.520
to see the intellectual property of Marvel&nbsp;
and the A-list talent of Chris Hemsworth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:28.240
at the center of a short film that could, with&nbsp;
the right equipment, be produced by any of us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.280
in our own apartments. This gives Team Thor a&nbsp;
homegrown, indie quality that's quite the contrast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.840
to the typically action-packed, effects-heavy&nbsp;
Marvel stories, even among the One-Shots.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.080
In this second installment, which came out&nbsp;
alongside the Blu-ray and digital releases of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.640
Doctor Strange, Thor is having trouble keeping&nbsp;
up his end of the rent alongside his roommate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.840
Darryl. After all, Thor only has Asgardian&nbsp;
money. So Thor hires an assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.355
who he pays in Asgard gold, to go out and get&nbsp;
a job so that he can pay Darryl. Nailed it.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:02.400
The last of the mockumentary-style One-Shots,&nbsp;
Team Darryl stars Jeff Goldblum reprising his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.680
role as Grandmaster from Thor: Ragnarok. It's a&nbsp;
wonderful creative exercise in showing a Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:13.280
character that's somehow even crazier than Thor&nbsp;
grounded in everyday life. He's presented without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:19.040
the fanfare or spectacle that most big-budget MCU&nbsp;
projects have. Goldblum is terrific and completely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:24.480
committed to the part. Given that Ragnarok was&nbsp;
his first and only appearance in the MCU thus far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.080
it's fun to have another opportunity&nbsp;
to see him shine as this character.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.280
Grandmaster has decided to take over Earth, and as&nbsp;
luck would have it, his first stop is Australia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:38.480
where he moves in with Darryl, Thor's former&nbsp;
roommate from the Team Thor One-Shots. Amusingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:42.880
Darryl never makes the connection that&nbsp;
Grandmaster is an enemy of his former roommate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.040
nor does Grandmaster realize his new&nbsp;
home was previously occupied by Thor.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:52.240
Directed by Taika Waititi, Team Darryl came&nbsp;
with the home video release of Thor: Ragnarok.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:55.760
With streaming services on the rise&nbsp;
by then, many fans were no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:59.760
purchasing physical copies of movies&nbsp;
when this film was released, making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.821
Team Darryl tantalizing new content for those&nbsp;
who have yet to discover this gem on Disney+.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:08.400
Starring Sir Ben Kingsley as&nbsp;
Trevor Slattery, All Hail The King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.120
bridges the gap between Iron Man 3 and&nbsp;
Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:17.840
Of course, in true Marvel fashion, this came&nbsp;
out seven years before Shang-Chi debuted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:22.320
Marvel presented this One-Shot alongside the&nbsp;
home video release of Thor: The Dark World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.600
and it might just be better than&nbsp;
the feature film it was attached to.

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:30.320
After pretending to be the Mandarin, leader of&nbsp;
the terrorist group the Ten Rings, actor Trevor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:34.880
Slattery is in jail, where he's something&nbsp;
of a celebrity among his fellow prisoners.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.040
Eccentric and nostalgic, Trevor isn't&nbsp;
above reciting lines he made famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:43.360
as the fake Mandarin or reflecting&nbsp;
back on failed television pilots.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.560
"Fletcher. It's not something I can just turn on."

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.760
To Trevor's surprise, the real Mandarin actually&nbsp;
exists, and he'd like a word with the man who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:57.200
culturally appropriated and shamed his image. His&nbsp;
accomplices pose as documentary interviewers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.240
break Trevor out of prison — not to free him,&nbsp;
but to deliver him to the Mandarin himself.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.720
With a dedicated performance from Kingsley&nbsp;
and some fantastically elaborate cut-aways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.640
All Hail The King stands on its own as&nbsp;
more than just supplemental material.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:15.120
It even has a fun cameo from Sam Rockwell,&nbsp;
reprising his role as Justin Hammer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.494
a villain from Iron Man 2, living out&nbsp;
his sentence in the same jail as Trevor.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:24.640
The longest One-Shot to date at 15 minutes,&nbsp;
Agent Carter gives Hayley Atwell the opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:29.760
to shine as she carries Peggy Carter beyond the&nbsp;
confines of a supporting character and into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:35.040
role of a protagonist. Agent Carter came with&nbsp;
the Blu-ray and digital release of Iron Man 3.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:40.320
One year after Steve Rogers crashed his plane&nbsp;
and supposedly died, World War II is over and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:45.440
Peggy Carter works as the only female agent in&nbsp;
the office of the Strategic Scientific Reserve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:50.000
Though her male colleagues are sent into the field&nbsp;
to complete missions, all of her assignments are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.200
boring work. But when an emergency calls for&nbsp;
immediate action, Peggy accomplishes a mission&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.160
completely on her own. Howard Stark takes&nbsp;
notice and invites Peggy to come run SHIELD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.680
alongside him. This comes much to the dismay of&nbsp;
Peggy's sexist boss John Flynn, played by Bradley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:11.360
Whitford in his MCU debut, further proving&nbsp;
the credibility of the One-Shot program.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.600
"And Flynn, let her know that you're&nbsp;
honored to bring her the news."

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.560
This One-Shot served as a precursor&nbsp;
to the Agent Carter television series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:26.240
which premiered on ABC in 2015 and ran for&nbsp;
two seasons. It's legitimately entertaining,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:32.010
even for those with no familiarity with Marvel,&nbsp;
and delivers in spades for fans who love Peggy.

